# Bootstrap secret ONLY. Since 0.23.0 all other config (API keys, Google
# Drive OAuth, Fireflies, Gmail labels, Qdrant URL, port, etc.) lives in
# state/settings.json and is managed via the Settings UI tab.
#
# Why UI_SECRET stays here: it unlocks the UI itself. If it were in
# settings.json we'd have a chicken-and-egg bootstrap problem.
#
# Renamed from CAPTURE_SECRET → UI_SECRET in 0.24.0 — the old name was
# misleading once /capture stopped being the only thing it guarded.
#
# Setup: copy this file to repo root as `.env`, replace the value, then
# open the UI and fill the rest in Settings → categories below the MCP
# tokens section.

UI_SECRET=your-random-bootstrap-secret
